WEBVTT

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:35.690
<i>Hey...</i>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.540
<i>Hey, hey...</i>

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.570
<i>What's with the shape of its legs?</i>

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.400
<i>It... didn't actually fall.</i>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>It </i>jumped<i> here.</i>

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.840
<i>I... I totally don't want to do this.</i>

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.770
<i>But... this isn't the time 
to be saying that, I guess.</i>

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.220
Wh-Why you...!

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.520
Alex!

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.160
We're going after it!

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.530
Wh-Why?

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:57.090
Th-That's impossible...

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:04.680
W-We could... attack it from behind...

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.520
What?!

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.770
No... You've got to be kidding!

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.330
All right!

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>String.</i>

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.510
<i>There is a martial art that uses wire.</i>

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.570
<i>There are fibers that the army uses.</i>

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:53.330
<i>Various other organisms on Earth 
also incorporate the use of string.</i>

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.370
<i>Among them, the organism that 
creates the strongest string</i>

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:02.980
<i>doesn't make traps, or capture its prey with a net.</i>

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:07.870
<i>Instead, its livelihood depends on 
two strings that will not break.</i>

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.760
<i>Compared to a strand of spider silk of the same width,</i>

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:14.210
<i>this creature produces a string that 
can withstand 2.5 times more weight.</i>

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.920
<i>This insect...</i>

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:21.380
<i>is the Eumeta Japonica, 
which inhabits Japan.</i>

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.310
<i>It is an endangered species.</i>

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.340
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.520
I'm sorry that I left my post.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.530
I'm here to save you.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.030
<b><i>Martian Atmosphere and Roach Suitability Ranking</i></b>

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.030
<b>6TH</b>

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.070
<b>Hizamaru Akari</b>

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.330
By the way...

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.620
Are you all okay with bungee jumping?

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.290
Y-Yeah, that's fine, Akari-kun. 
I'm sure you have an id—

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.020
No! No way!

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:52.200
Even though you're kinda 
good looking, no!

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.740
<i>Now then...</i>

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.040
Your legs seem rather developed.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:10.090
Do cockroaches bulk up, too, 
if they run or do squats?

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.980
Or maybe you're doing Tantou.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.320
Nah...

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.130
Your legs are completely different.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.110
What are you...? A grasshopper?

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:37.310
<i>This is deep.</i>

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:42.260
<i>This thing's hands seem to have 
suckers on them, and I can't get away.</i>

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.760
<i>Its legs look like brushes, 
making it easier for him to swim.</i>

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.690
<i>Its back is shaped differently, too.</i>

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.760
<i>Its body is adapted for underwater battles.</i>

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.500
<i>It's not a cockroach...</i>

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:58.440
<i>Is it...</i>

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.820
<i>a diving beetle?</i>

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.820
<i>Five hundred years ago when they 
shipped the cockroaches off to Mars,</i>

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.830
<i>did diving beetles somehow get mixed in?</i>

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:13.000
<i>I'm surprised they survived, 
considering there was no water back then.</i>

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.830
<i>Apparently I have more of an 
imagination than I thought...</i>

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.020
<i>There's no way that could happen...!</i>

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.710
<b>2 Years Ago...</b>

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.280
<i>Is that someone from our 
parents' generation?</i>

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:06.730
<i>These things...</i>

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.890
<b>Did they...</b>

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:11.480
<b>Use the corpses...?</b>

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.130
I'm not gonna stop this airframe.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.710
I'm going to beat you within two minutes.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:40.320
<i>Nothing good has ever happened 
to me since I was born.</i>

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.960
<i>My father was already gone when I was born.</i>

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.170
<i>I got bullied because my 
home was so run-down...</i>

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:50.370
<i>And with men, I've only met uglies, 
or horrible hot guys or horrible old men!</i>

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.130
It's still early to be giving up, Yaeko.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.450
Right...

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.670
H-Huh?

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:08.300
<i>Sorry, Akari...</i>

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.180
<i>I don't think I'll be able 
to help you out for a while,</i>

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.530
<i>until I get everyone down safely...</i>

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:16.650
<i>It'll be fine. Akari...</i>

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:18.800
<i>is strong.</i>

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.740
<i>The battle was already over.</i>

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.680
<i>At that moment, Michelle had a 
feeling the cockroaches</i>

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.990
<i>were using the bodies of the Bugs 2 crew.</i>

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:56.650
<i>It's because she's so cunning that, 
at that moment, she was shaken.</i>

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:00.050
<i>It was also because she was shaken 
that she was dragged down so far.</i>

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:06.260
<i>The diving beetle's aerodynamic body 
has suckers on its front legs,</i>

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:07.980
<i>flippers for back legs,</i>

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:12.580
<i>and it also breathes in the special way 
unique to all underwater bugs.</i>

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:18.780
<i>It submerges itself by storing air in the 
space between its wings and its back,</i>

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.170
<i>but it doesn't merely consume this air.</i>

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:26.010
<i>When the oxygen is used, the emission 
of carbon dioxide increases,</i>

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.560
<i>and the carbon dioxide is exchanged 
with the oxygen in the water.</i>

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.740
<i>Therefore, it is possible for 
the diving beetle to survive in</i>

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:37.530
<i>the water for more than ten 
minutes without having any gills.</i>

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:44.320
<i>Michelle, on the other hand, 
is purely a land organism,</i>

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:46.030
<i>and her limit is two minutes.</i>

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.200
<i>Even with her bullet ant powers,</i>

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.640
<i>if her enemy's body temperature gets 
as cold as the water,</i>

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.290
<i>it is very possible they will not explode.</i>

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.340
<i>At this point, there is no 
way for Michelle to win.</i>

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.830
<i>If there is no way to win, Michelle...</i>

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:23.360
<i>will block her enemy's mobility,</i>

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.030
<i>squeeze with her legs as if they were a vise,</i>

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.170
<i>stop moving,</i>

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.120
<i>and count... two minutes.</i>

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.080
<b>Suffocation: Stage 1</b>

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.530
<i>For several seconds, your body will 
use the oxygen retained in the body.</i>

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.330
<i>Because of the carbon dioxide 
building within the blood,</i>

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.820
<i>you start experiencing severe pain.</i>

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.720
<b>Suffocation: Stage 2</b>

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:33.350
<i>Your blood pressure goes up, 
your muscles start to cramp, cyanosis.</i>

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.920
<i>Incontinence.</i>

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:41.230
<b>Suffocation: Stage 3</b>

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.900
<i>After things have progressed from stage 2,</i>

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.190
<i>you completely lose consciousness.</i>

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:49.850
<i>The cramping stops, 
and things become rather dire.</i>

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.930
<i>Cockroaches do not feel pain.</i>

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.260
<i>It's because it doesn't feel 
pain that it was perplexed</i>

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:01.500
<i>about why these legs, that are supposed 
to produce the utmost mobility</i>

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.350
<i>in the water, now couldn't 
move even a millimeter.</i>

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:09.320
<i>This worked in Michelle's favor.</i>

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.310
<i>If her enemy could feel pain,</i>

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:13.180
<i>it would have been screaming and writhing</i>

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.310
<i>in the hell-like pain it was experiencing.</i>

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:19.110
<i>If that had been the case, Michelle wouldn't 
have been able to stay so calm.</i>

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:24.320
<i>However, despite appearances, 
this move called the "figure-four leglock"...</i>

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:32.760
<i>It is said that if you endure it for 
two minutes, your bones will break.</i>

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:39.200
<i>However, even with her enhanced 
heart and lung functions,</i>

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:43.270
<i>after fighting for two minutes under water</i>

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:46.650
<i>Michelle did not have the 
ability to release the lock and</i>

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.400
<i>swim back to the surface.</i>

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:54.920
<i>Once suffocation reaches stage 
4, recovery is unlikely...</i>

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.390
<i>And once it progresses beyond that,</i>

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.770
<i>only death awaits.</i>

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.280
W-We're saved...

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.860
<i>The division leader still hasn't surfaced.</i>

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.070
<i>Akari's...</i>

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.240
<i>Crap!</i>

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.080
Are you surprised?

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:20.000
I heard that a grasshopper's legs

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:23.700
are powerful enough to jump over buildings 
when magnified to human size.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.810
And yet... "Why can't I break 
him? Why can't I kill him?

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:33.320
Why can't I rip apart this 
vermin?" I'm assuming?

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.510
I'll tell you why.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.820
It's because you're a roach.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:42.080
I'm assuming...

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.920
that the person who had the powers 
of a grasshopper on Bugs 2

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:48.150
was stronger than you.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:53.430
It's true that your strength, speed, 
and durability are all a threat.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:55.430
Not to mention

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:58.830
you understand how to operate the 
machines the humans left behind,

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.540
or you're being led by someone who does.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.800
And that leader apparently has 
has total command over you all.

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:13.110
Judging from the lack of hesitation 
in all your actions,

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.120
that leader has a vision.

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:22.380
That wisdom and power is also a threat.

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:24.410
Even then...

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:29.170
none of you have any experience fighting.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.050
Hey.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.050
What's the matter?

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:43.180
You can't kick me if I'm this close?

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.660
The first year, you learn your 
form and how to break logs.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.780
Start over!

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.260
Don't stand up.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.820
I'm not letting you stop this airframe.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.430
Since I adjusted the length...

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.050
Michelle-san...

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:26.730
should be just about done...

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:29.120
finishing off her enemy 
before her two minutes

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.500
of air run out.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:40.950
I see... He's pretty impressive.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.540
And now, stop!

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.300
Hey! I told you not to stand up!

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:10.550
I'm pretty sure that was the 
effect of inertia... I think.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.660
There's a lot of things you 
need to learn in science...

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:16.390
unlike language studies.

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:30.120
A jumping grasshopper is one thing,

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.760
but a cockroach with its wings 
spread is just a target.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:37.890
One more!

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:48.000
That one wasn't a bird ability.

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:53.560
That was the legendary magic ball, 
the curve, first performed in 1867,

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.360
and its Magnus effect.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.650
You won't find that on a test!

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.500
A transmission?

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:09.820
Which division is it from?

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:35.000
If I recall, the manual said 
non-combatants should go to

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.480
the escape vessel.

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:41.190
There aren't any non-combatants 
in this division.

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:56.870
All right. Let's go.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:01.260
We're going to stop Rahab's legacy.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.260
<b><i>Brave Warrior</i></b>
